i.github.com/users/Groovounet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Groovounet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/23149870","html_url":"https://github.com/g-truc/glm/issues/6#issuecomment-23149870","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/6","id":23149870,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzMTQ5ODcw","user":{"login":"nlguillemot","id":1079061,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzkwNjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1079061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot","html_url":"https://github.com/nlguillemot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-08-23T08:22:29Z","updated_at":"2017-08-09T00:21:45Z","body":"for any poor soul wandering upon this post in confusion,\r\n\r\nthe baryPosition output uses barycentric coordinates for the x and y components. The z component is the scalar factor for ray.\r\n\r\nThat is,\r\n\r\n1.0 - baryPosition.x - baryPosition.y = actual z barycentric coordinate\r\n\r\nif you compute the point inside the triangle that corresponds to those barycentric coordinates, you'll find the exact same answer as if you did:\r\norigin + direction \\* baryPosition.z\r\n\r\ntl;dr:\r\n```\r\n[ v0.x v1.x v2.x ]   [ baryPosition.x ]\r\n[ v0.y v1.y v2.y ] * [ baryPosition.y ]\r\n[ v0.z v1.z v2.z ]   [ (1.0 - baryPosition.x - baryPosition.y) ]\r\n```\r\n\r\nis equal to\r\n\r\norigin + direction \\* baryPosition.z\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/23149870/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"nlguillemot","id":1079061,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzkwNjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1079061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot","html_url":"https://github.com/nlguillemot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nlguillemot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/68117855","html_url":"https://github.com/g-truc/glm/issues/6#issuecomment-68117855","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/6","id":68117855,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY4MTE3ODU1","user":{"login":"evg-zhabotinsky","id":6692701,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2OTI3MDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6692701?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/evg-zhabotinsky","html_url":"https://github.com/evg-zhabotinsky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evg-zhabotinsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evg-zhabotinsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evg-zhabotinsky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evg-zhabotinsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evg-zhabotinsky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evg-zhabotinsky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evg-zhabotinsky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evg-zhabotinsky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/evg-zhabotinsky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-12-26T01:38:28Z","updated_at":"2014-12-26T02:31:07Z","body":"Well, I feel it is exactly the way it should work, but should not it be documented?\nI've noticed that sum of baryPosition coordinates is not 1 but really could not understand what the hell is going on until I've read the above explanation.\n**EDIT:** _as of version 0.9.6.1:_\nIn fact barycentric coordinates are **[(1 - bary.x - bary.y); bary.x; bary.y]**, which is a bit counter-intuitive.\nSo intersection result is as follows:\nv0 * (1 - bary.x - bary.y) + v1 * bary.x + v2 * bary.y\n= origin + direction * bary.z\n= intersection coordinates (cartesian)\nAlso, triangle vertices must go counter-clockwise when looking along the ray for them to intersect.\n(That is, in context of OpenGL, only front face of triangle intersects the ray, not the back one.)\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api